course: dictionary
lesson: 3830
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A formula is a rule written with letters, numbers or symbols. In maths, it tells you how to work something out, like area = length × width. Put in the numbers and you get the answer.
explain: The word can also mean a set of steps that brings a certain result. «When the three disagree, a thinker has to weigh the reasons on each side; there is no simple formula.» Here the author is not talking about sums at all. The words «weigh the reasons» show it is about thinking, so a formula means an easy set of steps that always works. Saying there is no simple formula means there is no easy set of steps that always gets the answer.
explain: Use the context clues around the word to choose the right meaning. Words like maths, chemical or baby tell you which meaning fits. Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A formula is a rule written with letters and symbols, such as area = length × width.
fact: In science, a chemical formula shows what a substance is made of, using letters and numbers: H2O is water.
fact: «Formula» can also mean powdered milk made for feeding babies.
fact: Formula One is a class of motor racing.
fact: «Formula» can mean a set of steps that brings a certain result, as in «a formula for success». The plural can be formulas or formulae.
exercise: «When the three disagree, a thinker has to weigh the reasons on each side; there is no simple formula.» In this sentence, what does formula mean? | *A set of steps or a rule that always gives the result | A race between fast cars | A child's toy made of wood | A bottle of milk for a baby
exercise: In maths, area = length × width is a formula. What is a formula here? | A drawing of a shape | A word for a long race | *A rule with letters and symbols that tells you how to work something out | A letter that stands for a number
exercise: In chemistry, H2O is a formula. What does it show? | A sum of money | *What a substance is made of, written with letters and numbers | The name of a racing car | A baby's milk
test: Which meaning of formula is about feeding babies? | A class of motor racing | A rule for working something out | *Powdered milk made for feeding babies | A set of steps for success
test: Ella says formula only ever means a maths rule. Is she right? | Yes, it only means a race | Yes, it only means a maths rule | No, it means a country | *No, it has several meanings, including baby milk and Formula One
exam: What does «a formula for success» mean? | Powdered milk for babies | *A set of steps that brings a good result | A rule written with letters and numbers | A type of motor race
